SEG = 'PAY'
CAT = 'cbcsPayers'
Q = [
("A child's parents are married. Mother born March 4, 1985; father born January 20, 1990. Whose plan is primary?",
 "The father's plan", ["The mother's plan", "The older parent's plan", 'The plan enrolled first'],
 "Under the NAIC coordination of benefits model, the birthday rule uses only the month and day. January 20 comes before March 4, so the father's plan pays first."),
("A woman has coverage through her own job and as a dependent on her husband's plan. Which pays first for her?",
 "Her own employer's plan", ["Her husband's plan", 'The plan of the older spouse', 'The spouse born earlier in the year'],
 'Under the NAIC model, the plan covering the person as an employee (non-dependent) pays before the plan covering her as a dependent.'),
('A man is covered as an active employee by one plan and as a retiree by another. Which is primary?',
 'The active-employee plan', ['The retiree plan', 'The plan held longer', 'The plan of the larger employer'],
 'The NAIC rule for active versus retired or laid-off employees makes the plan covering the person as an active employee primary.'),
('A patient has a group plan through his current job and COBRA coverage from a former job. Which pays first?',
 'The current job plan', ['The COBRA plan', 'The plan held longer', 'The plan with the earlier birthday'],
 'Under the NAIC model, a plan covering a person as an employee is primary over continuation coverage such as COBRA.'),
('A child lives with her father, but a court decree makes her mother responsible for health care. Whose plan is primary?',
 "The mother's plan", ["The father's plan", "The custodial parent's plan", "The older parent's plan"],
 "Under the NAIC model, when a court decree assigns responsibility for the child's health care, that parent's plan pays first, whatever the custody arrangement."),
('Divorced parents share joint custody, and the decree does not say who covers health care. What decides the primary plan?',
 'The birthday rule', ["The custodial parent's plan", "The father's plan", 'The plan with the lower deductible'],
 'The NAIC model applies the birthday rule when a decree gives joint custody without assigning health care responsibility.'),
("Which group does the Children's Health Insurance Program cover?",
 'Uninsured kids above Medicaid limits', ['Children who qualify for Medicaid', 'Children of federal civilian workers', 'Children of active-duty troops'],
 'CHIP, funded jointly by states and the federal government, covers uninsured children in families whose incomes are too high for Medicaid but who cannot afford private coverage.'),
('Which part of Original Medicare covers a walker ordered for home use?',
 'Part B', ['Part A', 'Part C', 'Part D'],
 'Durable medical equipment for use at home falls under Medicare Part B, the medical insurance part.'),
('Medicare covers hospice care under which part?',
 'Part A', ['Part B', 'Part C', 'Part D'],
 'Hospice is a Part A (hospital insurance) benefit, as are inpatient stays and skilled nursing facility care.'),
('What must happen before Part A covers a skilled nursing facility stay?',
 'A 3-day inpatient stay', ['A 3-day observation stay', 'A 1-day inpatient stay', 'A 3-day ER and observation stay'],
 'Medicare.gov states SNF coverage requires a prior medically necessary inpatient hospital stay of at least 3 days in a row; observation and ER time do not count.'),
('A patient picks Option 2 on an ABN. What has she chosen?',
 'Service, no Medicare claim', ['Service, with a Medicare claim', 'To refuse the service', 'To bill her Medigap plan first'],
 'Option 2 means she wants the item or service but does not want Medicare billed, and she pays. Option 1 asks for a Medicare claim; Option 3 declines the service.'),
('May a Medicare patient be asked to sign an ABN during a medical emergency?',
 'No, not under duress', ['Yes, before treatment starts', 'Yes, if a family member signs', 'Yes, if she can still sign'],
 'Medicare Claims Processing Manual chapter 30 says a notice should not be obtained in a medical emergency or under great duress, since the patient cannot make a rational choice.'),
('A patient with Medicare and full Medicaid gets an ABN. Which option must she be told to check?',
 'Option 1', ['Option 2', 'Option 3', 'Options 1 and 2'],
 'Medicare Claims Processing Manual chapter 30 says dually eligible beneficiaries must be told to check Option 1 so the claim goes to Medicare for a decision.'),
('One plan has no coordination of benefits provision; the other does. Which is usually primary?',
 'The plan without the provision', ['The plan with the provision', 'The plan held longer', 'The plan with the lower premium'],
 'Under the NAIC model, a plan that lacks a coordination of benefits provision consistent with the regulation is always primary, unless both plans say the complying plan is.'),
('A patient is enrolled in the QMB program. What may the office bill her for Medicare cost sharing?',
 'Nothing', ['Coinsurance only', 'Deductible only', 'Full charges'],
 'Federal law bars Medicare providers from billing Qualified Medicare Beneficiaries for Medicare deductibles, coinsurance or copayments.'),
('A nonparticipating physician bills Medicare. Which claims must still be filed on assignment?',
 'Clinical lab services', ['Office visits', 'Minor office surgery', 'Chest X-ray readings'],
 'Medicare Claims Processing Manual chapter 1, section 30.3.1, mandates assignment for clinical diagnostic laboratory services, among others, regardless of participation.'),
("An employer pays its workers' claims from its own funds instead of buying insurance. What is this?",
 'Self-funded plan', ['Fully insured plan', 'Community-rated plan', 'Group indemnity plan'],
 'In a self-funded plan the employer bears the claim risk, often with a third-party administrator. A fully insured plan buys a policy from an insurer.'),
('What must go with a paper claim to the secondary payer?',
 "The primary payer's EOB", ["The primary payer's referral", "A copy of the patient's card", "The primary claim's superbill"],
 'The secondary payer needs to see what the primary allowed, paid and left to the patient before it can coordinate its own payment.'),
('A patient has three plans. When is the tertiary payer billed?',
 'After the secondary pays', ['Along with the primary', 'Before the secondary', 'Only if all others deny'],
 "Claims go in order: primary, then secondary with the primary's results, then tertiary with both prior results."),
('Who qualifies for Medicare before age 65?',
 'People with ESRD', ['People with type 1 diabetes', 'People with stage 3 CKD', 'People on short-term disability'],
 'Besides people 65 and older, Medicare covers people with end-stage renal disease and those who have received Social Security disability benefits for 24 months.'),
]
